From: Michael R Sweet <msweet@msweet.org>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] backend/ipp: sanitize IPP attribute strings in quote_string()
 (CVE-2026-55453)

Backport of upstream OpenPrinting/cups fix for CVE-2026-55453 /
GHSA-7hqf-mfhx-7r3v (2.4.x commit d41cf06, master commit 806e1b48):
"ipp backend status-line injection can update queue PPD and lead to
conditional RCE as lp via foomatic-rip".

backend/ipp.c quote_string() copies remote-supplied IPP string attribute
values into the "ATTR: name=\"...\"" / "STATE:" status lines written to the
backend's stdout, but did not neutralize control characters. A malicious (or
MitM) IPP printer can put CR/LF inside job-printer-state-message /
printer-state-message (and other reported text attributes) to break out of the
current line and inject additional ATTR:/STATE:/PPD: scheduler records. Those
are consumed by scheduler/statbuf.c -> update_job(), which then lets the remote
persistently update the queue PPD and (where a PPD-driven filter such as
foomatic-rip is in the chain) can lead to execution as the filter account.

Fix (matching upstream, defense at the source emitter): inside quote_string()'s
copy loop, map every control character ((unsigned char) < 0x20) and DEL (0x7f)
to a single space instead of copying it verbatim, so a reported value can never
introduce a new backend status line. This is complementary to the already
backported scheduler-side hardening (option-value control-char filtering and
the "PPD:" special-keyword blacklist); neither alone closes the emitter.

Adaptation to 2.4.14: applies to backend/ipp.c quote_string() only; hunk line
numbers reflect the build state after the existing install.py patch chain
(cups-log-datamasking/ohos_ip_conflict/cups-ipp-multifile shift this function's
offset but do not touch its body). Verified with git apply --fuzz=0 on that
chain.

Upstream-commit: d41cf0616688721e9d435d54118c4c8a36ed596a
Upstream-commit: 806e1b483 (master equivalent)
CVE: CVE-2026-55453
GHSA: GHSA-7hqf-mfhx-7r3v

diff --git a/backend/ipp.c b/backend/ipp.c
index f11421c5..eef49980 100644
--- a/backend/ipp.c
+++ b/backend/ipp.c
@@ -3156,7 +3156,20 @@ quote_string(const char *s,		/* I - String */
         break;
     }
 
-    *qptr++ = *s++;
+    if ((*s & 255) < ' ' || *s == 127)
+    {
+     /*
+      * Replace control characters (incl. CR/LF/TAB) and DEL with a
+      * space, so a remote IPP attribute value cannot inject extra
+      * backend status lines (ATTR:/STATE:/PPD:) nor break the quoted
+      * option grammar...  (CVE-2026-55453)
+      */
+
+      *qptr++ = ' ';
+      s ++;
+    }
+    else
+      *qptr++ = *s++;
   }
 
   *qptr++ = '\"';
